@baseUrl = https://localhost:7179
@adminEmail = utkucakar@hotmail.com
# Type your AdminUser:Password (user secrets) here while testing. Do not commit it
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME

### 1) Login: access token in the body, refresh token in an HttpOnly cookie (see the Set-Cookie response header)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 2) Wrong password -> 401, same message as an unknown email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 3) Admin endpoint without a token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers

### 4) Admin endpoint with the token -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 5) Refresh: new access token, new refresh token cookie (rotation).
### Paste the refreshToken value from the last Set-Cookie header (the part between "refreshToken=" and the first ";")
### Sending the same value a second time -> 401, and the newer token stops working too (reuse detection)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Cookie: refreshToken=PASTE_HERE

### 6) Refresh without the X-Requested-With header -> 400 (CSRF, second layer)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Cookie: refreshToken=PASTE_HERE

### 7) Logout: the refresh token stops working, the cookie is cleared
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Cookie: refreshToken=PASTE_HERE
